Verse 1:
[Bbm]Come let us [Ab]sing of homeland,
[Ab]Down [Bbm]by [Eb7]the crystal sea;
[Ab]Wonderful [Db]land where [Bbm]Jesus
[Eb7/Bb]Buildeth [Ab]a [Eb/Bb]mansion for me.

Refrain:
[Eb]Over [Ab]yonder, down by the crystal sea,
[Eb7]Over yonder, there's [Ab]where I long to be,
[Ab]No more sorrow, [Db/Ab]toil, grief, [Ab]nor care,
[Cm]In the homeland [Fm]bright [Bbm/Db]and [Db]fair,
[G7/D]Over, [Ab/Eb]over there.

Verse 2:
[Bbm]Water [Ab]of life there floweth,
[Ab]Fruit [Bbm]in [Eb7]abundant store;
[Ab]Citizens [Db]of that [Bbm]country
[Eb7/Bb]Hunger [Ab]and [Eb/Bb]thirst never more.

Verse 3:
[Bbm]Come go with [Ab]me to homeland,
[Ab]Jesus [Bbm]invites [Eb7]you there;
[Ab]Help spread [Db]the invitation,
[Eb7/Bb]Tell [Ab]it to [Eb/Bb]men everywhere.
